{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdZSo95JLCK69sdPgRUv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've rewritten the repair candidate, `signed_personal_decisiveness`, and it passes the self-check. That check is a one-chain smoke test, so it doesn't measure convergence. It is still unknown whether the repair fixes what got the first attempt rejected (R-hat 1.53, bulk ESS 7).\n\n**Hypothesis:** each person has one signed decisiveness. Most people follow their impression of which sequence looks more random, some barely do, and a few do the reverse and pick the less random one. That single trait accounts for why people agree with the majority choice to such different degrees, which is the gap the critique found. It replaces personal guessing rates.\n\n**What I changed for the repair:**\n- **Likely cause of the bad fit:** the old model multiplied each person's signed decisiveness by personal weights on imbalance and on the longest streak. Each person's sign and scale could then swap between the two factors and give the same fit, so the sampler had several equally good answers to wander between.\n- **The fix:** those two weights are now shared by everyone. Only each person's ideal switching rate and their decisiveness are personal, which is also a simpler model.\n- I also tightened the prior on how much decisiveness varies between people (from 1.0 to 0.7).\n- `hypothesis.md` and the model's docstring now describe this version.\n\n**Check result:** `OK`, with an ELPD-LOO of -3730.5 on the 100-draw smoke fit; the incumbent's full fit is -3470.5, though a smoke fit isn't a fair comparison. The check also warned that PSIS-LOO is unreliable: 7.3% of trials have Pareto k above 0.5, against a 1% tolerance. A smoke fit that short may cause this. If it persists in the full fit, it could stop the model from being exported as the winner even if it is admitted.\n\n**Not checked:**\n- **Convergence:** this machine has one CPU, and the smoke fit alone took about 2 minutes (the whole check about 5), so I didn't run a multi-chain test.\n- **Fit time:** I haven't checked it against the 30-minute admission limit.\n- **Novelty:** I haven't checked it against the existing models.\n\nThis is the slot's last attempt; another rejection is final.\n\nThe three files are in `experiment3/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_2_repair_1/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":485,"cache_read_input_tokens":87806,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":485,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":697,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a81be7ff-c485-4db4-8482-222777cdd695","uuid":"abe46ae8-f215-45d5-98ec-453ae9c772f6","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:22:26.063Z","request_id":"req_011CfdZSnjWvUSoEstucsYXF"}
